================================================================================
Additions by the MCP-Injector authors
================================================================================

The following components are original contributions of the MCP-Injector
authors (see AUTHORS) and are released under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  - The MCP-Injector proxy middleware, including the fault-injection
    operators (OP0_nullInjector, OP1_smallDelta, OP2_randomValue,
    OP3_randomWrongType, OP4_errorMessage, OP5_delay, OP6_dropCall)
    and their persistence model (PERMANENT, TRANSIENT, INTERMITTENT).
  - The calibration pipeline under mining/ (five notebooks plus supporting
    scripts) that mines open-source MCP repositories, classifies threads,
    and produces the empirical fault profile consumed by
    fault_modes/fault_mode_1.json.
  - The campaign orchestration scripts (run_campaign.sh, run_op0_baseline.sh,
    run_no_inj_baseline.sh) and the fault-mode profile selector logic in the
    runner.
  - The failure audit and rerun tooling under analysis/failure_audit/.
  - The analysis pipeline and figure-generation code under analysis/.

================================================================================
Data artifacts
================================================================================

Data artifacts released with this repository are distributed under a separate
license (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International, CC-BY-4.0). Data
artifacts are defined as:

  - fault_modes/fault_mode_0.json (null profile, used as the OP0 condition).
  - fault_modes/fault_mode_1.json (calibrated profile, used as the OPP
    condition, empirically grounded in the mined corpus).
  - analysis/results_formatted/fault_mode_1_fired_faults.csv (per-call
    log of fired faults from the reported campaigns).
  - All per-task result JSONs under analysis/results_formatted/ (the 1,350
    cells that constitute the primary evidence base for RQ1 through RQ7).
  - The per-thread classifier outputs of the calibration pipeline under
    mining/ (CSV and XLSX; fields: thread identifier, deterministic
    thread_url, repository metadata, failure_mode, failure_persistence).
    Raw issue and PR narratives are deliberately not shipped.

